{"results":[{"id":"9514daa5-7d47-4214-a5ca-d9d906ac44c3","ino":"1688849860322953","oldLibraryItemId":null,"libraryId":"afaa178b-e2a9-4b8c-b80f-e592faca091d","folderId":"58c29b46-e133-465a-905c-92b15f0536ed","path":"F:/Books/Philip Pullman/The Book of Dust/2 - The Secret Commonwealth","relPath":"Philip Pullman/The Book of Dust/2 - The Secret Commonwealth","isFile":false,"mtimeMs":1732972987834,"ctimeMs":1732972987834,"birthtimeMs":1732972987823,"addedAt":1732973000348,"updatedAt":1765843526650,"isMissing":false,"isInvalid":false,"mediaType":"book","media":{"id":"dc6af3a5-77a4-4fff-82df-e527cfa865d5","metadata":{"title":"The Book of Dust: the Secret Commonwealth (Book of Dust, Volume 2)","titleIgnorePrefix":"Book of Dust: the Secret Commonwealth (Book of Dust, Volume 2), The","subtitle":null,"authorName":"Philip Pullman","authorNameLF":"Pullman, Philip","narratorName":"","seriesName":"The Book of Dust #2","genres":["Belacqua, Lyra (Fictitious character)"],"publishedYear":"2019","publishedDate":null,"publisher":"Random House Large Print","description":"Lyra Silvertongue thought the adventures of her youth were long over, but when her daemon, Pantalaimon, witnesses a brutal murder, they are suddenly caught up in crimes that carry unsettling echoes from their past. But Lyra at twenty is very different from Lyra at thirteen. The lies she used to spin with ease no longer come, she and Pan are at odds, and her ability to trust -- most of all in herself -- has been shattered. On the run, Lyra finds a surprising new ally in Malcolm Polstead. Lyra and Malcom will travel far beyond the confines of Oxford, across Europe and into the Levant, searching for a city haunted by daemons, and a desert said to hold the mystery of Dust. To find the truth, Lyra will have to reconnect with the girl she once was and face dangers that will challenge everything she knows about her world.","isbn":"9780593340875","asin":null,"language":"eng","explicit":false,"abridged":false},"coverPath":"C:/Users/alxno/AppData/Local/Audiobookshelf/metadata/items/9514daa5-7d47-4214-a5ca-d9d906ac44c3/cover.jpg","tags":[],"numTracks":0,"numAudioFiles":0,"numChapters":0,"duration":0,"size":5221274,"ebookFormat":"epub"},"numFiles":1,"size":5221274},{"id":"b306d895-98f9-49a5-a65f-2e2c9df6f767","ino":"1125899906914033","oldLibraryItemId":null,"libraryId":"afaa178b-e2a9-4b8c-b80f-e592faca091d","folderId":"58c29b46-e133-465a-905c-92b15f0536ed","path":"F:/Books/Philip Pullman/The Book of Dust/1 - La Belle Sauvage","relPath":"Philip Pullman/The Book of Dust/1 - La Belle Sauvage","isFile":false,"mtimeMs":1765747953682,"ctimeMs":1765747953682,"birthtimeMs":1732973029582,"addedAt":1732973052170,"updatedAt":1765843526613,"isMissing":false,"isInvalid":false,"mediaType":"book","media":{"id":"f71d7bca-efd9-43eb-8ae2-6e09b963514d","metadata":{"title":"La Belle Sauvage: The Book of Dust Volume One","titleIgnorePrefix":"La Belle Sauvage: The Book of Dust Volume One","subtitle":"From the world of Philip Pullman's His Dark Materials - now a major BBC series","authorName":"Philip Pullman","authorNameLF":"Pullman, Philip","narratorName":"","seriesName":"The Book of Dust #1","genres":["Juvenile Fiction"],"publishedYear":"2017","publishedDate":null,"publisher":"Random House","description":"WINNER- AUTHOR OF THE YEAR, BRITISH BOOK AWARDS SHORTLISTED- UK AUTHOR CATEGORY, NATIONAL BOOK AWARDS 2018 Philip Pullman's magnificent bestseller is now in paperback, with new additional illustrations. A coming of age story like no other . . . Malcolm Polstead's Oxford life has been one of routine, ordinary even. He is happiest playing with his daemon, Asta, in their canoe, La Belle Sauvage. But now as the rain builds, the world around Malcolm and Asta is, it seems, set to become increasingly far from ordinary. Finding himself linked to a baby by the name of Lyra Belacqua, Malcolm is forced to undertake the challenge of his life and to make a dangerous journey that will change him and Lyra for ever . . .","isbn"