blishedYear":"2009","publishedDate":null,"publisher":"Random House","description":"In Invisible Cities Marco Polo conjures up cities of magical times for his host, the Chinese ruler Kublai Khan, but gradually it becomes clear that he is actually describing one city: Venice. As Gore Vidal wrote 'Of all tasks, describing the contents of a book is the most difficult and in the case of a marvelous invention like Invisible Cities, perfectly irrelevant.'","isbn":null,"asin":null,"language":"en","explicit":false,"abridged":false},"coverPath":"C:\\Users\\alxno\\AppData\\Local\\Audiobookshelf\\metadata\\items\\59d59a3e-623f-484c-93eb-ee1b6250b5a4\\cover.jpg","tags":[],"numTracks":0,"numAudioFiles":0,"numChapters":0,"duration":0,"size":423699,"ebookFormat":"epub"},"numFiles":2,"size":427315},{"id":"a9f61547-f5e7-4a54-880f-6c71397bc4ae","ino":"1688849860283197","oldLibraryItemId":null,"libraryId":"afaa178b-e2a9-4b8c-b80f-e592faca091d","folderId":"58c29b46-e133-465a-905c-92b15f0536ed","path":"F:/Books/Ted Chiang","relPath":"Ted Chiang","isFile":false,"mtimeMs":1765842204488,"ctimeMs":1765843513449,"birthtimeMs":1765749237411,"addedAt":1765749061337,"updatedAt":1766361611355,"isMissing":false,"isInvalid":false,"mediaType":"book","media":{"id":"178adc8e-1785-459d-8895-7b741918e497","metadata":{"title":"Exhalation","titleIgnorePrefix":"Exhalation","subtitle":null,"authorName":"Ted Chiang","authorNameLF":"Chiang, Ted","narratorName":"","seriesName":"","genres":["Relato, Ciencia ficción"],"publishedYear":"2019","publishedDate":null,"publisher":"ePubLibre","description":"From the acclaimed author of Stories of Your Life and Others – the basis for the Academy Award nominated film Arrival – comes a groundbreaking second collection of short fiction: nine stunningly original, provocative, and poignant stories. In ‘The Merchant and the Alchemist’s Gate’, a portal through time forces a fabric-seller in ancient Baghdad to grapple with past mistakes and the temptation of second chances. In the epistolary ‘Exhalation’, an alien scientist makes a shocking discovery with ramifications not just for his own people, but for all of reality. And in ‘The Lifecycle of Software Objects’, a woman cares for an artificial intelligence over twenty years, elevating a faddish digital pet into what might be a true living being. Also included are two previously unpublished stories: ‘Omphalos’ and ‘Anxiety Is the Dizziness of Freedom’. In Exhalation, Ted Chiang wrestles with the oldest questions on earth – what is the nature of the universe? What does it mean to be human? – and ones that no one else has even imagined. And, each in its own way, the stories prove that complex and thoughtful science fiction can rise to new heights of beauty, meaning, and compassion.","isbn":null,"asin":null,"language":"en","explicit":false,"abridged":false},"coverPath":"C:\\Users\\alxno\\AppData\\Local\\Audiobookshelf\\metadata\\items\\a9f61547-f5e7-4a54-880f-6c71397bc4ae\\cover.jpg","tags":[],"numTracks":0,"numAudioFiles":0,"numChapters":0,"duration":0,"size":1377337,"ebookFormat":"epub"},"numFiles":2,"size":1381620},{"id":"5234d948-7c79-4421-9b15-57ea18febcca","ino":"1688849860283199","oldLibraryItemId":null,"libraryId":"afaa178b-e2a9-4b8c-b80f-e592faca091d","folderId":"58c29b46-e133-465a-905c-92b15f0536ed","path":"F:/Books/China Miéville","relPath":"China Miéville","isFile":false,"mtimeMs":1765749292263,"ctimeMs":1765843513306,"birthtimeMs":1765749282407,"addedAt":1765749201666,"updatedAt":1765843526018,"isMissing":false,"isInvalid":false,"mediaType":"book","media":{"id":"7beda4e7-73e3-4f39-9733-5d5c66d19abc","metadata":{"title":"The City & The City","titleIgnorePrefix":"City & The City, The","subtitle":null,"authorName":"China Miéville","authorNameLF":"Miéville, China","narratorName":"","seriesName":"","genres":[],"publishedYear":"2009","publishedDate":null,"publisher":"Ballantine Books","description":null,"isbn":"978-0-345-51566-7","asin":null,"language":"en-US","explicit":false,"abridg